{# extract_triples.j2 — Schema-constrained triple extraction for the KG #}
Extract subject-predicate-object triples from the text below.
Use ONLY predicates from this controlled vocabulary:
{{ controlled_predicates | join(', ') }}

For each triple:
- subject: canonical entity name
- predicate: from the vocabulary above ONLY
- object: canonical entity name or value
- fact_id: the source fact this triple derives from
- temporal_qualifier: ISO date or period if stated (optional)

Rules:
1. Use the controlled predicate vocabulary exactly as listed.
2. Resolve entity aliases to their canonical form (e.g. "NTRO", "the Organisation" -> "NTRO").
3. Do NOT create triples for facts not in the source.

Output JSON: { "triples": [ {subject, predicate, object, fact_id, temporal_qualifier?} ] }

Source facts:
{% for fact in facts %}
[{{ fact.fact_id }}] {{ fact.canonical_text }}
{% endfor %}
